# ── Node / frontend build artifacts ─────────────────────────────
.nodeenv/
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── macOS app build artifacts (build-macos.sh) ───────────────────
# .build-venv/ self-ignores today only because `python -m venv` writes its
# own internal `.gitignore` (`*`) — that's an accident of the venv tool, not
# a repo rule, and doesn't cover a BUILD_VENV pointed elsewhere. dist-app/
# (the frozen .app + .dmg) and .build-work/ (PyInstaller's workpath) had no
# rule at all and showed up as untracked after every build.
#
# .build-python/ is the standalone CPython the venv is built FROM. It lives
# here rather than in /tmp because the venv caches an absolute path to its
# base interpreter in `pyvenv.cfg`: when that path is transient, the venv
# survives the interpreter and every later build dies inside pip with
# "No module named 'encodings'" — a failure that names neither the venv nor
# the missing Python. Both are re-provisionable; they rot together.
.build-venv/
.build-python/
.build-work/
dist-app/

# ── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pixi/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# ── Runtime user projects (app-generated: networks, pickles, uploaded TS) ──
# These are written by the running backend, not source. They contain binary
# NetCDF blobs and pickled solver state — never belongs in version control,
# especially a public repo.
# NOTE: this entry ALSO covers per-project chat.jsonl files written by the
# chatbot integration (chat_service.append_turn writes to
# backend/projects/<name>/chat.jsonl) — no additional gitignore line needed.
backend/projects/

# ── Secrets / API keys (chatbot integration v6) ──
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and any other env-loaded credentials live in .env files,
# loaded by the backend process at startup. NEVER commit these.
.env
.env.local
.env.*
!.env.example
# Checked-in Vite dev default so `npm run dev` shows login on this branch
# without requiring a local .env.local. Override with .env.local if needed.
!.env.development

# Local SQLite auth DB used for Docker-less review
backend/auth_dev.db
backend/*.db
# WAL sidecars. The backend now opens file-backed SQLite in WAL mode, which
# creates `<db>-shm` and `<db>-wal` alongside it — `*.db` does not match those.
backend/*.db-shm
backend/*.db-wal

# ── Never commit pickles (deserialisation = code-exec risk on clone) ──
*.pkl

# ── Solver / scratch output ─────────────────────────────────────
*.log
WindowsTemp*.json
response.json

# ── OS / editor cruft ───────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
